# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the admin-dashboard React + Vite application.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (npm)
- Package version added to dependencies in package.json

### 2. Code Integration
**Modified: `src/App.tsx`**
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the root level inside `<BrowserRouter>`
- Component placed after all other provider wrappers to ensure proper initialization

### 3. Implementation Details
- **Framework**: React 19.2.4 with Vite 8.0.2
- **Integration approach**: React-specific implementation using `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- **Placement**: Component added outside all Refine providers but inside BrowserRouter, following best practices for analytics integration

### 4. Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (1.35s)
- ✅ No ESLint errors or warnings
- ✅ Speed Insights bundle properly code-split (vendor-vercel-speed-insights-DUywcHMn.js - 2.40 kB gzipped: 1.14 kB)
- ✅ No breaking changes to existing functionality

## Files Modified
1. `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
2. `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
3. `src/App.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component import and usage

## Next Steps
After deployment to Vercel:
1. Navigate to your Vercel dashboard
2. Select your project
3. Go to Speed Insights section
4. Click "Enable" to activate the feature
5. Speed Insights data will appear after deployment and user visits

## Technical Notes
- The integration follows the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart documentation (fetched on March 25, 2026)
- The component is framework-aware and automatically handles route tracking in React applications
- No additional configuration is required; the component works out of the box
- Data collection is GDPR compliant and privacy-focused
